<title>GERMANY: Daimler, Siemens top firm rankings.</title>
<headline>Daimler, Siemens top firm rankings.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business daily Handelsblatt on Monday reported the following rankings of the largest German corporations:</p>
<p>Top five in 1996 sales (in billions of marks):</p>
<p>    COMPANY		 SALES     PCT CHNG   INDUSTRY</p>
<p>    Daimler-Benz AG	106.3	  +3	cars, aerospace</p>
<p>    Volkswagen AG	  100.1	 +14	cars</p>
<p>    Siemens AG		94.2	  +6	diverse industry</p>
<p>    Veba AG		   68.1	  +3	utility, telecom</p>
<p>    Deutsche Telekom AG   63.1	  +6	telecom</p>
<p>Top five in 1996 net profit (in billions of marks):</p>
<p>    COMPANY		NET PROFIT  PCT CHNG    INDUSTRY</p>
<p>    Siemens AG		2.990	 +43     diversified</p>
<p>    BASF AG		   2.790	 +13     chemicals</p>
<p>    Hoechst AG		2.774	 +24     chemicals</p>
<p>    Daimler-Benz AG	 2.762	 --*     cars, aerospace</p>
<p>    Bayer AG		  2.747	 +13     drugs, chemicals</p>
<p>* Daimler-Benz's1996 net profit came after a 1995 loss of 5.729 billion marks.</p>
<p>Top five in worldwide employees:</p>
<p>    COMPANY		    NO. OF EMPLOYEES	 INDUSTRY</p>
<p>    Siemens AG		    379,000		 diversified</p>
<p>    Daimler-Benz AG	     290,000		 cars, aerospace</p>
<p>    Deutsche Bahn AG	    289,000		 railroads</p>
<p>    Deutsche Post AG	    285,000		 post office</p>
<p>    Volkswagen AG		 243,000		 cars</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
